# UX FEEDBACK LOOPS: INFINITY PROTOCOL v8.4.0

> **UX SOVEREIGNTY**: The system must ALWAYS acknowledge user intent instantly. Silence is a failure state.

## 1. The "Zero-Latency" Illusion (Optimistic UI)
- **Principle**: UI updates immediately; Server syncs in background.
- **Requirement**: ALL mutations must have an optimistic update or immediate visual feedback.

```tsx
// ✅ FUNCTIONAL PATTERN: Optimistic UI with React 19 / SWR
import { useOptimistic } from 'react';

export function LikeButton({ serverLikes, onLike }) {
  const [optimisticLikes, addOptimisticLike] = useOptimistic(
    serverLikes,
    (state, current) => state + 1
  );

  return (
    <button 
      onClick={async () => {
        addOptimisticLike();    // Instant UI update
        await onLike();         // Background server sync
      }}
      className="active:scale-95 transition-transform"
    >
      {optimisticLikes} Likes
    </button>
  );
}
```

## 2. Notification Standards (Sonner)
- **Library**: `sonner` is the ABSOLUTE STANDARD for toasts.
- **Success**: Green/Teal. `toast.success("Action Completed")`
- **Error**: Red/Rose. `toast.error("Action Failed", { description: "Details..." })`
- **Loading/Promise**: Use `toast.promise` for async actions without optimistic UI.

```tsx
// ✅ FUNCTIONAL PATTERN: Async Toast Promise
import { toast } from 'sonner';

const handlePayment = async () => {
  toast.promise(processPayment(), {
    loading: 'Processing payment...',
    success: 'Payment successful! Receipt sent.',
    error: 'Payment failed. Please try again.',
  });
};
```

## 3. Micro-Interactions (Framer Motion)
- **Hover**: Elements must respond fluidly (`scale: 1.02`).
- **Click**: Buttons must depress (`scale: 0.95`, `active:scale-95`).
- **Transition**: Use `<AnimatePresence>` for mounting/unmounting. No abrupt DOM changes.

```tsx
// ✅ FUNCTIONAL PATTERN: Liquid Glass Interactive Button
import { motion } from 'framer-motion';

export const InteractiveButton = ({ children, onClick }) => (
  <motion.button
    whileHover={{ scale: 1.02 }}
    whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}
    onClick={onClick}
    className="px-6 py-2 rounded-xl bg-white/10 border border-white/20 backdrop-blur-md text-white shadow-[0_4px_24px_-8px_rgba(255,255,255,0.2)] hover:bg-white/20 transition-colors"
  >
    {children}
  </motion.button>
);
```

## 4. Skeleton States
- Never show a blank screen or unstyled raw data while loading.
- Use animated pulse skeletons matching the exact shape of the incoming data.

```tsx
// ✅ FUNCTIONAL PATTERN: Skeleton Pulse
<div className="w-full h-32 rounded-xl bg-white/5 animate-pulse border border-white/10" />
```

## 5. Global Toaster Configuration (Liquid Glass)
This component MUST be mounted in the Root Layout (`app/layout.tsx`) to ensure the `sonner` notifications adhere to the Infinity Protocol v8.4.0 aesthetic standard.

```tsx
// ✅ FUNCTIONAL PATTERN: providers/ToasterProvider.tsx
'use client';

import { Toaster } from 'sonner';

export function ToasterProvider() {
  return (
    <Toaster
      position="bottom-right"
      toastOptions={{
        className: 'bg-black/60 backdrop-blur-2xl border-white/10 text-white shadow-2xl rounded-2xl p-4',
        classNames: {
          error: 'text-rose-400 border-rose-500/30 bg-rose-500/10',
          success: 'text-teal-400 border-teal-500/30 bg-teal-500/10',
          warning: 'text-amber-400 border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10',
          info: 'text-blue-400 border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-500/10',
        },
      }}
    />
  );
}
```

