# ACCESSIBILITY GUARDIAN: INFINITY PROTOCOL v8.4.0

> **MANDATE**: Build for everyone. A site without a11y is a broken site. Radix Primitives / Shadcn are the standard.

## 1. SEMANTIC HTML & KEYBOARD SOVEREIGNTY

Building "div buttons" is a critical architecture failure.

```tsx
// ❌ REJECTED — div with onClick and no accessibility
<div onClick={handleClick}>Submit</div>

// ✅ REQUIRED — semantic button with keyboard support built-in
<button type="button" onClick={handleClick}>Submit</button>

// ✅ REQUIRED — focusable custom interactive element (rare)
<div 
  role="button" 
  tabIndex={0} 
  onClick={handleClick} 
  onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === 'Enter' && handleClick()}
  aria-label="Submit Form"
>
```

- **Focus Control**: `outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring` MUST be on all interactive elements.
- All `<img>` must have `alt`. Decorative images: `alt=""`.
- Use `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<section>` — not `<div>` wrappers.

## 2. RADIX PRIMITIVES MANDATE

Do not reinvent complex ARIA widgets. Use `@radix-ui` / `shadcn/ui`.

```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Radix Dialog (handles focus trap, esc to close, aria-modal implicitly)
import * as Dialog from '@radix-ui/react-dialog';

export const AccessibleModal = () => (
  <Dialog.Root>
    <Dialog.Trigger asChild>
      <button className="btn">Open Profile</button>
    </Dialog.Trigger>
    <Dialog.Portal>
      <Dialog.Overlay className="fixed inset-0 bg-black/50" />
      <Dialog.Content className="fixed bg-background p-6">
        <Dialog.Title>Edit Profile</Dialog.Title>
        <Dialog.Description>Make changes below.</Dialog.Description>
        <Dialog.Close />
      </Dialog.Content>
    </Dialog.Portal>
  </Dialog.Root>
);
```

## 3. ARIA REQUIREMENTS
| Element | Required ARIA |
|---|---|
| Icon-only button | `aria-label="Description"` |
| Input field | `<label htmlFor="id">` + matching `id` on input |
| Loading state | `aria-busy="true"` + `aria-live="polite"` on container |
| Error message | `role="alert"` + `aria-live="assertive"` |

## 4. MOTION SAFETY (Vestibular Defense)

Flashy animations can induce vertigo. Always respect OS-level motion reduction flags.

```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Framer Motion reduced-motion hook
import { motion, useReducedMotion } from 'framer-motion';

export const SafeAnimation = () => {
  const shouldReduceMotion = useReducedMotion();

  return (
    <motion.div
      initial={{ opacity: 0, y: shouldReduceMotion ? 0 : 20 }}
      animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
      transition={{ 
        duration: shouldReduceMotion ? 0.01 : 0.5, 
        ease: 'easeOut' 
      }}
    >
      Content
    </motion.div>
  );
};
```

## 5. COLOR & CONTRAST
- **Body text**: ≥ 4.5:1 contrast ratio (WCAG AA).
- **Large text / UI components**: ≥ 3:1 contrast ratio.
- **Never convey information via color alone** — pair with icon or text label.
